  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Big thanks to VRC devs for the update that literally nobody asked for, permanently killing mod support. You've just rendered my mute / hearing impaired friend completely unable to participate and communicate in the game because she was using mods that analyzed what people were saying and provided subtitles, and gave her a TTS interface to talk back. She's gutted over this, because VRC was her primary vehicle for social interaction.\n\nWhat you've done here is honestly one of the most unapologetically shitty things I've ever seen from a development team. Please, for christ's sake, listen to your community. Roll back the update. Ditch EAC. Embrace support for the modding community, or at least continue to tolerate it while you look for a better long term solution, because you're not just losing VRC+ subscribers at this point, you're deplatforming players entirely who rely on VRChat for more than just some silly fun.",
